[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2843665477","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105950#issuecomment-2843665477","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105950","id":2843665477,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6pfuRF","user":{"login":"raulsntos","id":3903059,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MDMwNTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3903059?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos","html_url":"https://github.com/raulsntos","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-30T23:27:38Z","updated_at":"2025-04-30T23:27:38Z","body":"There is a difference between a Span created from a null array and an empty array: [SharpLab](https://sharplab.io/#v2:EYLgxg9gTgpgtADwGwBYA0AXEUCuA7AHwAEAmARgFgAoagSzwwG0BdAfgAIBDKKTgTzLsAvOzw4ANuIDcdBi3Zce/EsPYsZNKgGUADpzwAeehgB87AM568gkd14CNu/UYZnL+lbaV8SG6kTIATgAKd2thETFJAEoNAJCwz0iJcVigA==)\r\n\r\n```csharp\r\nint[]? array1 = null;\r\nint[]  array2 = [];\r\n\r\nSpan<int> span1 = array1;\r\nSpan<int> span2 = array2;\r\n\r\nConsole.WriteLine(span1 == null); // Prints 'True'\r\nConsole.WriteLine(span2 == null); // Prints 'False'\r\n```\r\n\r\nSo the null check is not redundant and was added on purpose to catch cases where the user passes a null array.\r\n\r\nAlso, changing parameter types breaks compatibility.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2843665477/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2843668825","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105950#issuecomment-2843668825","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105950","id":2843668825,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6pfvFZ","user":{"login":"Joy-less","id":65855333,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1ODU1MzMz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65855333?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less","html_url":"https://github.com/Joy-less","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-30T23:30:31Z","updated_at":"2025-04-30T23:32:34Z","body":"> So the null check is not redundant and was added on purpose to catch cases where the user passes a null array.\r\n\r\nI didn't know this.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2843668825/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2843694352","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105950#issuecomment-2843694352","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105950","id":2843694352,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6pf1UQ","user":{"login":"Joy-less","id":65855333,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1ODU1MzMz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65855333?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less","html_url":"https://github.com/Joy-less","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-30T23:35:29Z","updated_at":"2025-04-30T23:39:04Z","body":"Nevermind @raulsntos I closed this too early. I think you have gotten confused here.\r\n\r\n```cs\r\nusing System;\r\n\r\nSpan<int> span = [];\r\n\r\nConsole.WriteLine(span == null); // Prints 'True'\r\n```\r\n[SharpLab](https://sharplab.io/#v2:EYLgxg9gTgpgtADwGwBYA0AXEUCuA7AHwAEAmARgFgAoagZQAcBDPAHgEs8MA+AAgGcmeHgF4eAbQC6AbmrUiZAJwAKAcxGi8OADZaAlFKA=)\r\n\r\nIn C#, converting a null array to a span always creates an empty but usable span. See the code:\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b3a8e690-6c19-4eb7-a4b3-8d07d4e6330f)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2843694352/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2874207241","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105950#issuecomment-2874207241","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105950","id":2874207241,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rUOwJ","user":{"login":"paulloz","id":437025,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNzAyNQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/437025?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz","html_url":"https://github.com/paulloz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulloz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-12T21:33:36Z","updated_at":"2025-05-12T21:33:36Z","body":"Hi. You're absolutely right that spans created from null arrays are functionally identical to spans created from empty arrays.\r\n\r\nI imagine what raulsntos was going for is that they can still be differentiated, and thus, we might want to purposefully design the API to not accept spans created from null arrays as a valid argument here.\r\n\r\nFor me, it's a matter of looking at how the BCL handles this kind of cases, and stick to it as long as it makes sense. I personally can't think of a method anywhere that'd treat both cases differently. Even this atrocity is valid C# code:\r\n```cs\r\nbyte[] array = ((Span<byte>)null).ToArray();\r\n```\r\nAnd `Span<T>.ToArray()` is probably the closest thing we'll find to the methods we're discussing.\r\n\r\nSo, long story short, I think we can merge this PR.\r\n\r\nI'm not entirely sure how breaking this is in terms of compatibility, since any previous call to `Array(Span<T> array)` should still be valid for `Array(ReadOnlySpan<T> span)`.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2874207241/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2874797443","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105950#issuecomment-2874797443","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105950","id":2874797443,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rWe2D","user":{"login":"raulsntos","id":3903059,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MDMwNTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3903059?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos","html_url":"https://github.com/raulsntos","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-13T01:54:52Z","updated_at":"2025-05-13T01:54:52Z","body":"> I'm not entirely sure how breaking this is in terms of compatibility, since any previous call to `Array(Span<T> array)` should still be valid for `Array(ReadOnlySpan<T> span)`.\r\n\r\nChanging the parameter type from `Span<T>` to `ReadOnlySpan<T>` maintains source compatibility since `Span<T>` is implicitly convertible to `ReadOnlySpan<T>`. But it breaks binary compatibility.\r\n\r\nChanging the name of the parameter from `array` to `span` breaks source compatibility because the callsite could be using named parameters (e.g.: `new Array<int>(array: [1, 2, 3])`) but we normally don't care too much about this.\r\n\r\nWe have to keep the `Array(Span<T> array)` constructors to avoid breaking binary compatibility. Breaking source compatibility is less disruptive.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2874797443/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2874953079","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105950#issuecomment-2874953079","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105950","id":2874953079,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rXE13","user":{"login":"Joy-less","id":65855333,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1ODU1MzMz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65855333?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less","html_url":"https://github.com/Joy-less","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-13T03:28:16Z","updated_at":"2025-05-13T03:28:16Z","body":"> We have to keep the `Array(Span<T> array)` constructors to avoid breaking binary compatibility. Breaking source compatibility is less disruptive.\r\n\r\n@raulsntos I added back the old constructors as deprecated and hidden, to be removed in the next major version of Godot. Let me know if you want something else.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2874953079/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2875066686","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105950#issuecomment-2875066686","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105950","id":2875066686,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rXgk-","user":{"login":"raulsntos","id":3903059,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MDMwNTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3903059?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos","html_url":"https://github.com/raulsntos","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-13T05:10:00Z","updated_at":"2025-05-13T05:10:00Z","body":"I don't think there's a reason to deprecate them, it will produce warnings when constructing from `T[]` or `Span<T>` which just adds noise.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2875066686/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2876313483","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105950#issuecomment-2876313483","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105950","id":2876313483,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rcQ-L","user":{"login":"Joy-less","id":65855333,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1ODU1MzMz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65855333?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less","html_url":"https://github.com/Joy-less","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-13T12:27:03Z","updated_at":"2025-05-13T12:27:03Z","body":"> I don't think there's a reason to deprecate them, it will produce warnings when constructing from `T[]` or `Span<T>` which just adds noise.\r\n\r\nIdeally this would be a good case for [OverloadResolutionPriorityAttribute](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/system.runtime.compilerservices.overloadresolutionpriorityattribute) but GodotSharp is targeting .NET 8.0. Removing the deprecations.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2876313483/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3303820279","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105950#issuecomment-3303820279","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105950","id":3303820279,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7E7Ev3","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-17T16:49:26Z","updated_at":"2025-09-17T16:49:26Z","body":"Thanks!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3303820279/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]